{"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is configured with one "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["PersistencePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    writers: [","        StateWriter(keyPath: \\.items) { writes, deletes in","            for item in writes { try? await db.upsert(item) }","            for id in deletes  { try? await db.delete(id: id) }","        },","    ],","    debounce: .milliseconds(250)  \/\/ Default; configurable",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called automatically through the plugin lifecycle — no manual invocation needed. Register the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and pass it to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s initializer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await store.flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" on shutdown ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scenePhase == .background"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"applicationWillTerminate"},{"type":"text","text":") to ensure buffered writes aren’t lost. This delegates to each registered plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}]},{"anchor":"Writer-Ordering","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Writer Ordering"},{"style":"warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writers flush sequentially in registration order."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If entity B references entity A via foreign key, A’s writer "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must"}]},{"type":"text","text":" come first. Otherwise B’s upsert looks up A’s row before it exists."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Warning"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register leaf entities first, aggregates last. Include a defensive fallback in upsert methods — if a referenced entity isn’t found, create it inline rather than setting the relationship to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Skip-the-boilerplate-SwiduxPersistence","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Skip the boilerplate: `SwiduxPersistence`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hand-wired form above (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":", plus a SwiftData"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow and a DB actor you write yourself) is the low-level path. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"}]},{"type":"text","text":" product turns it into a declare-and-register concern:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"annotate a domain entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and the macro generates its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shadow, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toDomain()"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" converters, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistableEntity"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator"},{"type":"text","text":" build the container, synthesize the writers, and reuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" under the hood — exposing only a merge-based"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-hydration path so a “refresh from disk” can’t clobber unflushed writes or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"live edits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"}]},{"type":"text","text":" layers opt-in iCloud sync on top: a runtime opt-out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toggle, launch-time entitlement\/account detection, and a merge-based"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remote-change observer. Linking it is the single signal that an app needs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iCloud\/CloudKit\/Push entitlements."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewa